AARON BLASIUS: Thank you, Krish.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:25.360
As you said, security
and data protection

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:28.615
are key to in cloud offering.

00:18:28.615 --> 00:18:31.420
As cloud adoption grows,
so too does the challenge

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:34.630
of keeping your cloud
workloads secure and protected.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:37.800
Security and data protection
are Google's top priority,

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.790
and our infrastructure
is designed, built,

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:43.030
and operated with into and
security is a core design

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:44.320
principle.

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:47.390
From the physical premises
to the purpose built servers,

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:50.710
networking equipment, security
chips, low level software

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:53.860
stack running on every
machine, our entire hardware

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:56.770
infrastructure is
Google-controlled, secured,

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:58.360
built, and hardened.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:01.680
And for many cases, the
security is transparent to you

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:02.850
as a customer.

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:06.850
But just by the virtue of
operating on Google GCP,

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:08.970
you are getting these benefits.

00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:11.470
Today, we'll be presenting a
number of exciting new features

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:14.860
in that area that we can
extend as a result of our end

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:17.860
to end security practices.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:22.000
The first is confidential VMs.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:26.490
Customers can run any workload
that they usually run in a VM.

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:28.640
And by clicking a
simple checkbox,

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:31.560
it will transform their
VM into a confidential VM.

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:34.650
Now all the memory pages
of the confidential VM

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:37.070
are inline encrypted.

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:40.700
The VMMemory it is
encrypted by a key per VM

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.320
and generated in hardware.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:44.240
This is an AMD
offering and we are

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:45.770
very excited to
partner with them

00:19:45.770 --> 00:19:47.448
in bringing this to market.

00:19:47.448 --> 00:19:49.490
And finally, the customers
can protect their data

00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:56.520
and to end in transit and
at rest as well as in use.

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:58.620
Shielded VMs are
also in GA, and this

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:01.160
is something I thought it would
be important to highlight.

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.210
Shielded VMs are
virtual machines

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:06.160
on Google Cloud hardened by
a set of security controls

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:11.550
that can help defend against
root kits and boot kit attacks.

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:13.980
The set of capabilities
ensure that your VM instances

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:17.210
have a healthy and
verified operating system.

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:19.530
It also means that protection
from malicious systems,

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:24.770
firmware, and guest operating
systems, tampering, et cetera--

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:27.480
we harden it against
those attacks.

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:30.490
We do this through security
features up and down the stack,

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:37.050
including UEFI firmware, secure
boot, and virtual trusted

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:39.070
platform or TPM.

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:41.955
These integrity
measures make it so

00:20:41.955 --> 00:20:43.830
that you can trust the
operating systems that

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:46.520
are running on cloud.

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:50.600
Additionally, we are
offering data protection.

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:52.880
Today, customers
have just one size

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:56.240
fits all option for data
management at a snapshot.

00:20:56.240 --> 00:20:59.840
Our goal for 2020 is to make
sure that copy data management

00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:02.630
that fits for workload goals.

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:04.380
If you don't want to
